  "_note": "on_kerb: tyres verified on the photo to lie on the kerb (apex markers). height: per-barrier override of wall_height_m (apex markers are single tyres lying flat, onboard video 27.07.2026). Kerb style: stripes (default, red/yellow), apron (red-dyed concrete pour with a light outer border, per the project author), concrete (plain grey concrete pour); both pours are raised 3 cm like a kerb but rumble less (own APRON surface). Kerbs start at the asphalt edge = the painted white edge line; they narrow to a point at their ends over taper_m = [start, end] metres (driving order; default kerb_taper_m in track.json) - extents and tapers measured on the 5 cm photo 2026-11-04, width = paint incl. its white border. extra_asphalt: any simple polygon; on 2026-11-04 re-traced from the 5 cm photo (asphalt grown from the hand-traced plates, at most 2.5 m beyond them, stopping at grass, soil and 0.6 m inside the track asphalt); plates run on under the tyres standing on them (tyre_ring sits on connector_e, inside included); connector_e, divider_end and connector_ne are old shortcuts between two straights: each side is the rounded end of the grass island next to it (a )( shape: from the island tip a quarter ellipse to each track, fitted to the grass edge on the 5 cm photo), running 0.8 m under the track. grid: the painted grid pattern relative to the start line (first row first_m before it, rows row_m apart, the second column stagger_m further back, lateral_m = lane centres left of the centreline; `painted` boxes are drawn, AC_START slots beyond continue the pattern). painted_lines: lane lines at a constant offset from the centreline, from_m..to_m before the start line (negative = after it). Both fitted to the orthophoto 2026-11-03 (residuals < 0.1 m, lanes 2.11 m apart). painted_cross: dashed lines across the asphalt at_m before the start line (the lanes end on one 4 m after it). Traced by hand from the GUGiK orthophoto (build/cache/ortho.bmp) on a 5 m grid, ~0.5-1 m accuracy; on 2026-11-04 most tyre barriers were snapped onto their tyre rows on the 5 cm 2026 photo (ortho_near: brightness contrast of a tyre-wide band, kept only where it sits clearly better on the tyres) - not snapped: on_kerb ones, start_tyre_pile, hairpin_c_divider (already on the tyres), start_east, tyre_pile_east (not detected). Local metres (x east, y north) as in centerline.csv. Edit and re-run `build.py validate` - check build/ortho_overlay.svg.",
